employee (reasonable relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (5/10).","financial_summary":["Republic Airways Holdings Inc. is a small-cap industrials business with a $942M market cap on $1.7B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +47% over the past three years, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at -10% against a 9% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The company is burning through $75M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 2.0\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and thin 2.8\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 33% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (1.3) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"ROIC sits in the bottom decile among Industrials peers \u2014 no moat advantage to speak of","sev":"red","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Industrials sector lagging the market significantly, underperforming by 6% over 3 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Cyclicality and capital intensity \u2014 order books turn on a dime, and the heavy fixed cost base that creates the moat also magnifies the downturn.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Supply chain reshoring costs and labour shortages \u2014 onshoring mandates raise capex requirements while a shrinking skilled-labour pool inflates operating costs.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Tariff and trade-policy exposure \u2014 industrial exporters sit squarely in the crosshairs of protectionist policy, and retaliatory tariffs c